{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the command-line interface and expands the core specification capabilities. The CLI now supports full Python expressions for specs and targets, while the library adds new tools for merging mappings and handling iteration.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The glom_cli tool must accept python-full format specifications that include arbitrary Python expressions rather than just AST literals. It must also support loading target data from Python files or strings using the python-full format."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The public API must expose the Merge spec and merge convenience function for combining iterables of mappings into a single mapping. Additionally, Spec instances used in key positions of default dict/mapping specs must evaluate their contents to enable dynamic key generation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure these features are properly documented and integrated into the main distribution package."
}
